{"kind": "ticker_day", "ticker": "MAIR", "date": "2026-08-25", "detectors": ["ep"], "old_paths": ["claude_classifier"], "old_match_paths": [], "old_grade": "mna", "old_decision": "BLOCK", "ep_day": true, "label": null, "arm": "ep: grader + headline", "corpus_source": "stored_grade_corpus", "corpus_len": 5040, "corpus": "[SEC 8-K filed 2026-08-25, items 1.01,3.02,7.01,9.01] mair-20260825 FALSE 0002098430 0002098430 2026-08-25 2026-08-25 UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION Washington, D.C. 20549 FORM 8-K CURRENT REPORT Pursuant to Section 13 or 15(d) of The Securities Exchange Act of 1934 Date of Report (Date of earliest event Reported): August 25, 2026 Madison Air Solutions Corporation (Exact name of registrant as specified in its charter) Delaware 001-43236 41-2529345 (State or other jurisdiction of incorporation or organization) (Commission File Number): (I.R.S. Employer Identification Number) 444 West Lake Street , Suite 4460 Chicago , IL 60606 (Address of principal executive offices) ( 312 ) 262-6374 (Registrant's telephone number, including area code) Check the appropriate box below if the Form 8-K filing is intended to simultaneously satisfy the filing obligation of the registrant under any of the following provisions: &#9744; Written communications pursuant to Rule 425 under the Securities Act (17 CFR 240.425) &#9744; Soliciting materials pursuant to Rule 14a-12 under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.14a-12) &#9744; Pre-commencement communications pursuant to Rule 14d-2(b) under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.14d-2(b)) &#9744; Pre-commencement communications pursuant to Rule 13e-4(c) under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.13e-4(c)) Securities registered pursuant to Section 12(b) of the Act: Title of each class Trading Symbol(s) Name of each exchange on which registered Class A common stock, par value $0.0000001 MAIR New York Stock Exchange Indicate by check mark whether the registrant is an emerging growth company as defined in Rule 405 of the Securities Act of 1933 (&#167;230.405 of this chapter) or Rule 12b-2 of the Securities Act of 1934 (&#167;240.12b-2 of this chapter). Emerging growth company &#9744; If an emerging growth company, indicate by check mark if the registrant has elected not to use the extended transition period for complying with any new or revised financial accounting standards provided pursuant to Section 13(a) of the Exchange Act. &#9744; Item 1.01 Entry into a Material Definitive Agreement. Securities Purchase Agreement On August 25, 2026, Madison Air Solutions Corporation (the &#8220;Company&#8221;) entered into a Securities Purchase Agreement (the &#8220;Institutional Investor Securities Purchase Agreement&#8221;) with certain institutional accredited investors named therein (each, an &#8220;Institutional Investor&#8221; and collectively, the &#8220;Institutional Investors&#8221;) and a Securities Purchase Agreement (the &#8220;Individual Securities Purchase Agreement&#8221; and, together with the Institutional Investor Securities Purchase Agreement, the &#8220;Securities Purchase Agreements&#8221;) with Larry Gies, pursuant to which the Company agreed to sell to the Institutional Investors and Mr. Gies, in a private placement (the &#8220;Private Placement&#8221;), an aggregate of 90,108,130 shares (the &#8220;Shares&#8221;) of the Company&#8217;s Class A common stock, par value $0.0000001 per share (the &#8220;Class A Common Stock&#8221;), at an offering price of $24.97 per Share. Mr. Gies, the Chairman of the board of directors of the Company (the &#8220;Board&#8221;) and sole manager of the Company&#8217;s controlling stockholder, Madison Industries Holdings LLC, has agreed to purchase $300.0 million of Class A Common Stock in connection with the Private Placement. Madison Solutions LLC (&#8220;Madison Solutions&#8221;), an entity affiliated with Mr. Gies, has also agreed to purchase $320.0 million of Class A Common Stock in connection with the Private Placement. The gross proceeds of the Private Placement are expected to be approximately $2.25 billion, before deducting applicable fees and other expenses. The Private Placement is expected to close on September 1, 2026, subject to the satisfaction of customary closing conditions (the &#8220;Closing&#8221;). The Company intends to use the net proceeds from the Private Placement to fully fund the equity portion \n\n[Benzinga 2026-08-25] Madison Air Solutions Announces $2.25B Private Placement Of 90,108,130 Shares At $24.97 Per Share.\n\n[Web summary] MAIR\u2019s latest gap-up catalyst was the market\u2019s reaction to its announced acquisition of German airflow specialist ebm-papst. The deal is being framed as a transformative move that nearly doubles Madison Air\u2019s addressable market and expands its airflow solutions portfolio, which is what\u2019s driving the renewed buying interest. [3]\n\nThe immediate news flow, however, has been mixed. On the announcement day, investors also focused on the fact that the acquisition would materially increase leverage and may require a secondary stock issue, which previously pressured the shares rather than boosted them. [2]\n\nSo if you\u2019re looking for the most recent \u201cwhy did it gap up\u201d explanation, it\u2019s deal-driven M&A optimism around ebm-papst, but the stock is still trading with a clear overhang from financing, integration, and execution-risk concerns. [3][2]\n\n", "headline_candidates_n": 0, "headline_article_cap": [], "fired_title_among_asked": false, "est_cost_usd_upper": 0.01309, "new_decision": null}
{"kind": "ticker_day", "ticker": "SOLS", "date": "2026-08-28", "detectors": ["ep"], "old_paths": ["veto_516"], "old_match_paths": [], "old_grade": "strong", "old_decision": "PASS", "ep_day": true, "label": null, "arm": "ep: grader + headline", "corpus_source": "stored_grade_corpus", "corpus_len": 5616, "corpus": "[SEC 8-K filed 2026-08-27, items 1.01,1.02,7.01,8.01,9.01] false 0002064953 0002064953 2026-08-27 2026-08-27 iso4217:USD xbrli:shares iso4217:USD xbrli:shares UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION WASHINGTON, D.C. 20549 Form 8-K CURRENT REPORT PURSUANT TO SECTION 13 OR 15(D) OF THE SECURITIES EXCHANGE ACT OF 1934 DATE OF REPORT &#8211; August 27, 2026 (Date of earliest event reported) SOLSTICE ADVANCED MATERIALS INC. (Exact name of Registrant as specified in its Charter) Delaware 001-42812 33-2919563 (State or other jurisdiction of incorporation) (Commission File Number) (I.R.S. Employer Identification Number) 115 Tabor Road Morris Plains , New Jersey 07950 (Address of principal executive offices) (Zip Code) Registrant&#8217;s telephone number, including area code: (973) 370-8188 Check the appropriate box below if the Form 8-K filing is intended to simultaneously satisfy the filing obligation of the registrant under any of the following provisions: &#168; Written communications pursuant to Rule 425 under the Securities Act (17 CFR 230.425) &#168; Soliciting material pursuant to Rule 14a-12 under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.14a-12) &#168; Pre-commencement communications pursuant to Rule 14d-2(b) under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.14d-2(b)) &#168; Pre-commencement communications pursuant to Rule 13e-4(c) under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.13e-4(c)) Securities registered pursuant to Section 12(b) of the Act: Title of each class Trading Symbol(s) Name of each exchange on which registered Common Stock, par value $0.01 per share SOLS The Nasdaq Stock Market LLC Indicate by check mark whether the registrant is an emerging growth company as defined in Rule 405 of the Securities Act of 1933 (&#167;230.405 of this chapter) or Rule 12b-2 of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 (&#167;240.12b-2 of this chapter). Emerging Growth Company &#168; If an emerging growth company, indicate by check mark if the registrant has elected not to use the extended transition period for complying with any new or revised financial accounting standards provided pursuant to Section 13(a) of the Exchange Act. &#168; Item 1.01 Entry into a Material Definitive Agreement. The information set forth in Item 1.02 below is hereby incorporated by reference into this Item 1.01. Item 1.02 Termination of Material Definitive Agreement. As previously disclosed, on July 6, 2026, Solstice Advanced Materials Inc., a Delaware corporation (&#8220;Solstice&#8221;), entered into an Agreement and Plan of Merger (the &#8220;Merger Agreement&#8221;) with Solar Merger Sub One Inc., a Delaware corporation and a wholly-owned subsidiary of Solstice (&#8220;Merger Sub One&#8221;), Solar Merger Sub Two LLC, a Delaware limited liability company and a wholly-owned subsidiary of Solstice (&#8220;Merger Sub Two&#8221;), and Element Solutions Inc, a Delaware corporation (&#8220;Element Solutions&#8221;). On August 27, 2026, Solstice, Merger Sub One, Merger Sub Two and Element Solutions entered into a Termination Agreement (the &#8220;Termination Agreement&#8221;) pursuant to which, among other things, Solstice and Element Solutions mutually terminated the Merger Agreement pursuant to Section 8.1(a) thereof. As a result, the Merger Agreement will be of no further force and effect. Subject to limited customary exceptions, the Termination Agreement also mutually releases the parties from any claims of liability to one another relating to the contemplated merger transaction. Under the terms of the Merger Agreement, neither Solstice nor Element Solutions will be responsible for any payments to the other party as a result of the termination of the Merger Agreement. The foregoing summary of the Termination Agreement is qualified in its entirety by the text of the Termination Agreement, a copy of which is attached as Exhibit 10.1 hereto and is incorporated herein by reference. The Merger Agreement, which was filed as Exhibit 2.1 to Amendment No. 1 to Current Report on Form 8-K/A filed by Solstice on July 9, 2026, is also incorporated herein by ref\n\n[Benzinga 2026-08-27] Trading Halt: Halt status updated at 5:25:00 PM ET: Quotation Resumption: News and Resumption Times.\n\n[Benzinga 2026-08-27] Solstice Advanced Materials' Board of Directors Authorizes $500M Share Repurchase Program; Co. Affirms Q3 And FY 2026 Guidance.\n\n[Benzinga 2026-08-27] Element Solutions Reveals Mutual Termination of Merger Agreement with Solstice Advanced Materials.\n\n[Web summary] SOLS gapped up because the company and Element Solutions mutually terminated their proposed $14.5 billion merger on August 27.\n\nInvestors viewed the cancellation positively because it removes the major risks that had pressured SOLS: substantial new debt, stock dilution, integration uncertainty, and leverage concerns. The deal had required significant financing and was expected to raise Solstice\u2019s net leverage to roughly 3.5 times EBITDA.\n\nThe second catalyst was Solstice\u2019s newly authorized $500 million share-repurchase program. The buyback signals management\u2019s confidence in the standalone business and gives the company a way to return capital to shareholders now that merger financing is no longer needed.\n\nSOLS also reaffirmed its raised 2026 guidance following its strong second-quarter report, which showed sales of $1.148 billion, up 11% year over year, and adjusted EBITDA of $290 million.\n\nThe immediate catalyst is therefore the merger termination plus the $500 million buyback, with reaffirmed guidance providing additional support. SOLS was indicated around $64\u201365 premarket versus a $56.34 close, roughly a 14%\u201316% gap higher.", "headline_candidates_n": 0, "headline_article_cap": [], "fired_title_among_asked": false, "est_cost_usd_upper": 0.01342, "new_decision": null}
{"kind": "ticker_day", "ticker": "CRK", "date": "2026-09-01", "detectors": ["ep"], "old_paths": ["veto_516"], "old_match_paths": [], "old_grade": "strong", "old_decision": "PASS", "ep_day": true, "label": null, "arm": "ep: grader + headline", "corpus_source": "stored_grade_corpus", "corpus_len": 1664, "corpus": "[Benzinga 2026-09-01] Comstock Resources Inks Letter Of Intent With State Oil Company Of Azerbaijan To Sell 20% Some Non-Operated Working Stake In Its Legacy Haynesville Upstream Assets, Western Haynesville Upstream Assets, Pinnacle Gas Services For $1.65B.\n\n[Web summary] CRK\u2019s gap-up was driven by a major strategic transaction announced Tuesday: Comstock Resources signed a letter of intent with Azerbaijan\u2019s state oil company, SOCAR.\n\nSOCAR would pay Comstock $1.65 billion in cash for non-operated interests in Comstock\u2019s Legacy Haynesville assets, Western Haynesville assets, and a portion of Comstock\u2019s stake in Pinnacle Gas Services. Comstock plans to use the proceeds primarily to reduce debt, potentially cutting net debt from about $3.1 billion to roughly $1.5 billion.\n\nThe deal also reduces Comstock\u2019s capital burden while allowing it to retain operational control of the assets. Separately, Comstock launched a roughly $450 million drilling venture with the Jones family partnership, which will fund much of the cost of drilling 27 Haynesville wells over the next year.\n\nThe market\u2019s immediate takeaway is balance-sheet improvement: substantially lower leverage, reduced financing pressure, and continued production growth without Comstock funding all the drilling itself. That is why the stock initially rose about 5% in premarket trading.\n\nImportant caveat: this is currently a letter of intent, not a completed sale. A definitive agreement is targeted by October 31, with closing expected by year-end, subject to approvals. The transaction also does not eliminate CRK\u2019s exposure to weak natural-gas prices, which hurt its latest quarterly revenue.", "headline_candidates_n": 0, "headline_article_cap": [], "fired_title_among_asked": false, "est_cost_usd_upper": 0.01115, "new_decision": null}
{"kind": "ticker_day", "ticker": "GPRK", "date": "2026-09-03", "detectors": ["ep"], "old_paths": ["claude_classifier"], "old_match_paths": ["claude_classifier"], "old_grade": "mna", "old_decision": "BLOCK", "ep_day": true, "label": "operator 2026-10-01: wrongly blocked", "arm": "ep: grader + headline", "corpus_source": "stored_grade_corpus", "corpus_len": 1958, "corpus": "[Benzinga 2026-09-03] Reported Earlier, GeoPark Expands Into Venezuela With New Position In Orinoco Oil Belt.\n\n[Benzinga 2026-08-28] 'Billionaire Gilinski, GeoPark Said to be Near Venezuela Oil Deal'- Bloomberg.\n\n[Web summary] GPRK gapped up primarily on GeoPark\u2019s announcement of a major strategic entry into Venezuela through the Bare Block, a producing heavy-oil asset in the Orinoco Heavy Oil Belt.\n\nKey details driving the move:\n\nGeoPark agreed to acquire Grupo Gilinski\u2019s 95% interest in the project by issuing roughly 42.1 million GPRK shares at $12.22 per share, a 26% premium to GeoPark\u2019s 30-day VWAP. The deal implies about $160 million, or approximately $1.50 per share, in immediate value accretion according to the company.\n\nGrupo Gilinski is expected to become GeoPark\u2019s controlling shareholder with roughly 56.3% ownership. GeoPark also plans a $100 million tender offer at $12.22 per share, giving existing shareholders a potential liquidity opportunity.\n\nThe Bare Block comes with a 25-year production participation contract with PDVSA, existing production and infrastructure, and substantial redevelopment potential. GeoPark says the project could eventually lift total production to approximately 70,000\u201383,000 barrels of oil equivalent per day and adjusted EBITDA to $925 million\u2013$1.3 billion by 2029\u20132030.\n\nThe announcement followed reports that GeoPark, Chevron and Eni were close to signing new Venezuelan energy agreements, so the market had already been speculating about the transaction. The formal company announcement converted that speculation into a definitive catalyst.\n\nThe main bullish interpretation is transformational production growth, entry into a potentially underinvested oil region, a premium-priced share issuance and the backing of Gilinski. The key risks are Venezuela political and sanctions exposure, execution and capital-spending requirements, heavy-oil economics, and significant dilution from the new shares.", "headline_candidates_n": 0, "headline_article_cap": [], "fired_title_among_asked": false, "est_cost_usd_upper": 0.01131, "new_decision": null}
{"kind": "ticker_day", "ticker": "IE", "date": "2026-09-08", "detectors": ["ep"], "old_paths": ["veto_516"], "old_match_paths": [], "old_grade": "strong", "old_decision": "PASS", "ep_day": true, "label": null, "arm": "ep: grader + headline", "corpus_source": "stored_grade_corpus", "corpus_len": 1181, "corpus": "[Web summary] Ivanhoe Electric (NYSE American: IE) appears to be gapping up primarily on renewed interest in its Santa Cruz copper project in Arizona.\n\nThe latest catalyst is a report that the U.S. Export-Import Bank has increased its potential financing support for Santa Cruz to approximately $1.1 billion, up from an earlier indication of $825 million. CEO Taylor Melvin also said the company is pursuing more than $1 billion in U.S.-backed debt and is targeting first copper production in 2029.\n\nThat financing prospect reduces the perceived need for heavily dilutive equity issuance and improves the project\u2019s chances of advancing into construction. The move is also being supported by broader strength in copper and strategic-minerals stocks.\n\nA secondary factor is institutional accumulation: Bank of New York Mellon disclosed a purchase of roughly 820,000 IE shares, worth about $7.9 million. However, the financing update is the more meaningful fundamental catalyst.\n\nKey risk: Santa Cruz still requires substantial capital, permitting and construction execution. The financing is not yet finalized, so the gap could fade if definitive debt commitments do not materialize.", "headline_candidates_n": 0, "headline_article_cap": [], "fired_title_among_asked": false, "est_cost_usd_upper": 0.01088, "new_decision": null}
{"kind": "ticker_day", "ticker": "OBX", "date": "2026-09-08", "detectors": ["ep"], "old_paths": ["veto_516"], "old_match_paths": [], "old_grade": "routine", "old_decision": "PASS", "ep_day": true, "label": null, "arm": "ep: grader + headline", "corpus_source": "stored_grade_corpus", "corpus_len": 1213, "corpus": "[Web summary] OBX\u2019s gap-up appears tied to the recent completion of Obsidian Therapeutics\u2019 reverse merger with Galera Therapeutics and the company\u2019s transition to Nasdaq trading under the OBX ticker on August 4.\n\nThe key catalyst is investor interest in Obsidian\u2019s engineered TIL immunotherapy platform, particularly OBX-115. Earlier clinical data showed a 67% objective response rate in advanced melanoma, including complete and partial responses, with no treatment-related mortality or major reported safety signals in the reported cohort.\n\nThere is also a technical/supply factor: Obsidian raised $350 million in a private placement connected with the merger. Those PIPE shares were reportedly expected to become tradable in September, which can create substantial volatility as investors position ahead of, or react to, the registration and release of additional shares.\n\nSo the move appears driven by a combination of renewed attention after the merger, optimism around OBX-115 clinical data, and low-float/speculative trading\u2014not a clearly identified new clinical announcement released today. Be cautious: the newly tradable PIPE shares could increase selling pressure and make the gap difficult to sustain.", "headline_candidates_n": 0, "headline_article_cap": [], "fired_title_among_asked": false, "est_cost_usd_upper": 0.0109, "new_decision": null}
