FWDI The NASDAQ Capital Market Indicate by check mark whether the registrant is an emerging growth company as defined in Rule 405 of the Securities Act of 1933 (17 CFR &#167;230.405) or Rule 12b-2 of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 (17 CFR &#167;240.12b-2). Emerging growth company &#9744; If an emerging growth company, indicate by check mark if the registrant has elected not to use the extended transition period for complying with any new or revised financial accounting standards provided pursuant to Section 13(a) of the Exchange Act. &#9744; Item 7.01. Regulation FD Disclosure. On September 15, 2026, Forward Industries, Inc. (the &#8220;Company&#8221;) issued a press release announcing its updated proposal to acquire SkyAI, Inc. A copy of the press release is furnished as Exhibit 99.1 to this Current Report on Form 8-K and is incorporated herein by reference. The information in this Item 7.01, including Exhibit 99.1 attached hereto, is being furnished and shall not be deemed &#8220;filed&#8221; for purposes of Section 18 of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 (the &#8220;Exchange Act&#8221;), or otherwise subject to the liabilities of that section. The information in this Item 7.01 and Exhibit 99.1 shall not be incorporated by reference into any filing under the Securities Act of 1933, or the Exchange Act, except as shall be expressly set forth by specific reference in such a filing. Item 9.01. Financial Statements and Exhibits. (d) Exhibits Exhibit No. Exhibit Description 99.1 Press Release, dated September 15, 2026 (furnished herewith) 104 Cover Page Interactive Data File (embedded within the Inline XBRL document) 2 SIGNATURES Pursuant to the requirements of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934, the registrant has duly caused this report to be signed on its behalf by the undersigned hereunto duly authorized. FORWARD INDUSTRIES, INC. Date: September 15, 2026 By: /s/ Michael Pruitt Name: Michael Pruitt Title: Interim Chief Executive Officer 3\n\n[EX-99] EX-99.1 2 forward_ex9901.htm PRESS RELEASE Exhibit 99.1 Forward Industries Announces Updated Proposal to Acquire SkyAI, Inc. Proposal reflects a 50% premium to SkyAI&rsquo;s closing price on September 14, 2026. SkyAI stockholders may elect cash or Forward common stock, or any combination of the two. AUSTIN, Texas, Sep 15, 2026 (Globe Newswire) -- Forward Industries, Inc. (NASDAQ: FWDI) (the &ldquo;Company&rdquo; or &ldquo;Forward&rdquo;), the leading Solana treasury company, today announced that it has delivered a letter to the Board of Directors of SkyAI, Inc. proposing to acquire all of SkyAI&rsquo;s issued and outstanding common stock. Under the proposal, SkyAI stockholders would receive cash and/or shares of Forward common stock, at each holder&rsquo;s election. Each SkyAI share would be converted into the value of 0.306 Forward shares, a fixed exchange ratio that would not adjust for changes in the trading price of either company&rsquo;s common stock. Based on the closing price of $6.95 per Forward share on September 14, 2026, the ratio implies consideration of $2.13 per SkyAI share, a 50% premium to SkyAI&rsquo;s closing price of $1.42 on the same date. Forward has proposed to effect the transaction as a merger or other tax-efficient combination as the parties may mutually agree. &ldquo;Our updated offer reflects our conviction in the value this combination can create,&rdquo; said Ryan Navi, CIO of Forward Industries. &ldquo;Forward has a proven playbook and a track record of execution that delivers value. SkyAI&rsquo;s stockholders have waited long enough. We&rsquo;re ready to move quickly - the next step is for the Board to engage.&rdquo; Forward has requested a response from the SkyAI Board by 5:00 p.m. Eastern time on September 25, 2026. The proposal is non-binding and remains subject to customary conditions, including completion of due diligence, the negotiation and execution of a definitive agreement, receipt of required regulatory approvals, and approval by SkyAI&rsquo;s stockholders. There can be no assurance that any transaction will be agreed or completed, or that any definitive agreement will be entered into. No Offer or Solicitation This press release is for informational purposes only. It does not constitute an offer to sell or the solicitation of an offer to buy any securities, nor is it a solicitation of any vote or approval, and the", "headline_candidates_n": 0, "headline_article_cap": [], "fired_title_among_asked": false, "est_cost_usd_upper": 0.01364, "new_decision": null}
{"kind": "ticker_day", "ticker": "JBS", "date": "2026-09-18", "detectors": ["ep"], "old_paths": ["claude_classifier"], "old_match_paths": ["claude_classifier"], "old_grade": "mna", "old_decision": "BLOCK", "ep_day": true, "label": "operator 2026-10-01: wrongly blocked", "arm": "ep: grader + headline", "corpus_source": "stored_grade_corpus", "corpus_len": 5559, "corpus": "[SEC 8-K filed 2026-09-15, items 8.01,9.01] false 0001791942 0001791942 2026-09-15 2026-09-15 iso4217:USD xbrli:shares iso4217:USD xbrli:shares UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION WASHINGTON, D.C. 20549 FORM 8-K CURRENT REPORT Pursuant to Section 13 or 15(d) of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 Date of Report (Date of earliest event reported): September 15, 2026 JBS N.V. (Exact name of registrant as specified in its charter) Netherlands 001-42678 98-1861274 (State or other jurisdiction of incorporation) (Commission File Number) (IRS Employer Identification No.) Stroombaan 16, 5th Floor Amstelveen , Netherlands 1181 VX (Address of principal executive offices) (Zip Code) + 31 20 656 47 00 (Registrant&#8217;s telephone number, including area code) N/A (Former name or former address, if changed since last report) Check the appropriate box below if the Form 8-K filing is intended to simultaneously satisfy the filing obligation of the registrant under any of the following provisions ( see General Instruction A.2): &#9744; Written communications pursuant to Rule 425 under the Securities Act (17 CFR 230.425) &#9744; Soliciting material pursuant to Rule 14a-12 under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.14a-12) &#9744; Pre-commencement communications pursuant to Rule 14d-2(b) under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.14d-2(b)) &#9744; Pre-commencement communications pursuant to Rule 13e-4(c) under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.13e-4(c)) Securities registered pursuant to Section 12(b) of the Act: Title of each class Trading Symbol(s) Name of each exchange on which registered Class A common shares, par value &#8364;0.01 per share JBS New York Stock Exchange Indicate by check mark whether the registrant is an emerging growth company as defined in Rule 405 of the Securities Act of 1933 (&#167;230.405 of this chapter) or Rule 12b-2 of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 (&#167;240.12b-2 of this chapter). Emerging growth company &#9744; If an emerging growth company, indicate by check mark if the registrant has elected not to use the extended transition period for complying with any new or revised financial accounting standards provided pursuant to Section 13(a) of the Exchange Act. &#9744; Item 8.01. Other Events. On September 15, 2026, JBS N.V.&#8217;s (&#8220;JBS&#8217;s&#8221;) wholly-owned Brazilian subsidiary JBS S.A. (&#8220;JBS S.A.&#8221;) entered into a Brazilian law-governed association agreement (the &#8220;Association Agreement&#8221;) with Viva Holding Ltda. (&#8220;Viva Holding&#8221;) (JBS S.A. and Viva Holding, individually a &#8220;Party&#8221; and collectively, the &#8220;Parties&#8221;), with Vanz Holding Ltda. (&#8220;Vanz&#8221;) and Viposa Participa&#231;&#245;es Ltda. (&#8220;Viposa&#8221; and, together with Vanz, the &#8220;Viva Shareholders&#8221;), as consenting intervening parties and guarantors, and Viva S.A. (&#8220;Viva&#8221;) and JBS Couros Brasil Ltda. (&#8220;JBS Couros&#8221;), as consenting intervening parties. The Association Agreement sets forth the definitive terms and conditions under which, following the satisfaction of certain conditions, the Parties will consummate the combination of the assets and activities related to the production, processing and commercialization of leather of JBS S.A. and Viva, through a company to be named &#8220;JBS Viva&#8221; (the &#8220;Transaction&#8221;). The Association Agreement sets forth the following principal terms and conditions: (i) JBS Viva will be owned, immediately after closing (&#8220;Closing&#8221;), in equal parts by JBS S.A. and Viva Holding, each of which will own 50% of the shares issued by JBS Viva. JBS S.A. will subscribe for the new common shares issued by JBS Viva and will pay for them by contributing all of the quotas issued by JBS Couros, a company that will hold all of the assets of JBS S.A.&#8217;s leather division; (ii) Before Closing, corporate reorganizations will be carried out to (a) concentrate in Viva Holding the ownership of all shares of Viva and segregate the assets and activiti\n\n[Web summary] JBS N.V. (NYSE: JBS) appears to be gapping up primarily on renewed attention to its proposed acquisition of the remaining publicly traded shares of Pilgrim\u2019s Pride (NASDAQ: PPC).\n\nJBS offered 2.086 JBS Class A shares for each PPC share in an all-stock, nonbinding proposal. JBS already owns roughly 82% of Pilgrim\u2019s Pride, so completing the transaction would consolidate the subsidiary and potentially lead to PPC\u2019s delisting. PPC shares rallied sharply on the proposal, and investors are viewing the deal as potentially value-enhancing for JBS through greater control and operational consolidation.\n\nThe secondary catalyst is the broader beef-price backdrop. U.S. cattle inventories remain historically tight, keeping beef prices elevated and supporting JBS\u2019s pricing power, although proposed U.S. beef-import measures and policies encouraging smaller ranchers to process beef are limiting the upside and have caused volatility in meatpacker stocks.\n\nThe JBS Viva leather venture, announced September 15, is positive strategically but is probably not the main reason for the gap. It would combine JBS and Viva leather operations in a 50/50 company, but the deal remains conditional and disclosed no immediate financial consideration.\n\nBottom line: the likely gap-up catalyst is the Pilgrim\u2019s Pride consolidation proposal, with tight cattle supplies and elevated beef prices providing additional support. Be careful not to confuse JBS with JBSS, John B. Sanfilippo & Son, which is a different stock.", "headline_candidates_n": 0, "headline_article_cap": [], "fired_title_among_asked": false, "est_cost_usd_upper": 0.01337, "new_decision": null}
{"kind": "ticker_day", "ticker": "BRSL", "date": "2026-09-21", "detectors": ["ep"], "old_paths": ["veto_516"], "old_match_paths": [], "old_grade": "routine", "old_decision": "PASS", "ep_day": true, "label": null, "arm": "ep: grader + headline", "corpus_source": "stored_grade_corpus", "corpus_len": 1191, "corpus": "[Web summary] BRSL\u2019s gap-up catalyst appears to be its appearance at the NASPL 2026 conference in Orlando, running September 21\u201324. Brightstar is showcasing its lottery technology and content portfolio, which likely renewed investor interest in its North American lottery business and potential customer opportunities.\n\nThe more substantial recent company news is the completed debt-refinancing activity: Brightstar accepted \u20ac342.2 million of its 2028 notes for repurchase, leaving \u20ac157.8 million outstanding, funded partly through a new \u20ac500 million 4.875% senior secured note due 2032. That extends the maturity profile and reduces near-term refinancing pressure, although it increases interest expense.\n\nBottom line: the immediate gap-up driver is most likely NASPL conference visibility and expectations around product/customer announcements, while the refinancing news provides a secondary balance-sheet tailwind. I did not see evidence in the available news of a new earnings release, acquisition, contract award, or regulatory catalyst driving the move. Be cautious about chasing it if the stock is moving on conference speculation rather than a disclosed contract or guidance change.", "headline_candidates_n": 0, "headline_article_cap": [], "fired_title_among_asked": false, "est_cost_usd_upper": 0.01089, "new_decision": null}
{"kind": "ticker_day", "ticker": "FWDI", "date": "2026-09-21", "detectors": ["ep"], "old_paths": ["veto_516"], "old_match_paths": [], "old_grade": "routine", "old_decision": "PASS", "ep_day": true, "label": null, "arm": "ep: grader + headline", "corpus_source": "stored_grade_corpus", "corpus_len": 1329, "corpus": "[Web summary] FWDI\u2019s gap-up catalyst was renewed takeover speculation around SkyAI, not earnings.\n\nForward Industries updated its non-binding proposal to acquire all of SkyAI on September 15. The revised offer values SkyAI at approximately $2.13 per share, a 50% premium to SkyAI\u2019s September 14 close. SkyAI holders could choose cash, FWDI shares, or a combination, based on a fixed exchange ratio of 0.306 FWDI shares for each SkyAI share.\n\nThe stock\u2019s subsequent surge\u2014roughly 24% to around $7.70\u2014appears to reflect traders repricing FWDI on expectations that the higher offer could advance, along with broader strength in Solana- and crypto-linked equities. Forward is positioning itself as a Solana treasury company, so the crypto rally also amplified the move.\n\nThe key caveat is that the SkyAI offer remains non-binding. It requires due diligence, a definitive agreement, regulatory approvals, and SkyAI shareholder approval. SkyAI had previously rejected Forward\u2019s proposal and supported pursuing its standalone strategy. Forward requested a response from SkyAI\u2019s board by 5:00 p.m. ET on September 25.\n\nBottom line: the immediate catalyst is the sweetened SkyAI acquisition bid, with Solana/crypto momentum adding fuel. The move is speculative and could reverse sharply if SkyAI rejects the proposal or negotiations fail.", "headline_candidates_n": 0, "headline_article_cap": [], "fired_title_among_asked": false, "est_cost_usd_upper": 0.01097, "new_decision": null}
{"kind": "ticker_day", "ticker": "VKTX", "date": "2026-09-22", "detectors": ["9m_sugar_baby", "ep"], "old_paths": ["polygon_news"], "old_match_paths": ["title"], "old_grade": "strong", "old_decision": "BLOCK", "ep_day": true, "label": "operator 2026-10-01: wrongly blocked", "arm": "ep: grader + headline", "corpus_source": "stored_grade_corpus_first_6000", "corpus_len": 6000, "corpus": "[SEC 8-K filed 2026-09-22, items 8.01,9.01] 8-K 0001607678 false 0001607678 2026-09-22 2026-09-22 UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION WASHINGTON, D.C. 20549 FORM 8-K CURRENT REPORT Pursuant to Section 13 or 15(d) of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 Date of Report (Date of earliest event reported): September 22, 2026 Viking Therapeutics, Inc. (Exact name of Registrant as Specified in Its Charter) Delaware 001-37355 46-1073877 (State or Other Jurisdiction of Incorporation) (Commission File Number) (IRS Employer Identification No.) 9920 Pacific Heights Blvd, Suite 500 San Diego , California 92121 (Address of Principal Executive Offices) (Zip Code) Registrant&#8217;s Telephone Number, Including Area Code: 858 704-4660 (Former Name or Former Address, if Changed Since Last Report) Check the appropriate box below if the Form 8-K filing is intended to simultaneously satisfy the filing obligation of the registrant under any of the following provisions: &#9744; Written communications pursuant to Rule 425 under the Securities Act (17 CFR 230.425) &#9744; Soliciting material pursuant to Rule 14a-12 under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.14a-12) &#9744; Pre-commencement communications pursuant to Rule 14d-2(b) under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.14d-2(b)) &#9744; Pre-commencement communications pursuant to Rule 13e-4(c) under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.13e-4(c)) Securities registered pursuant to Section 12(b) of the Act: Title of each class Trading Symbol(s) Name of each exchange on which registered Common Stock, par value $0.00001 per share VKTX The Nasdaq Stock Market LLC Indicate by check mark whether the registrant is an emerging growth company as defined in Rule 405 of the Securities Act of 1933 (&#167;&#8239;230.405 of this chapter) or Rule 12b-2 of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 (&#167;&#8239;240.12b-2 of this chapter). Emerging growth company &#9744; If an emerging growth company, indicate by check mark if the registrant has elected not to use the extended transition period for complying with any new or revised financial accounting standards provided pursuant to Section 13(a) of the Exchange Act. &#9744; Item 8.01 Other Events. On September 22, 2026, Viking Therapeutics, Inc. issued a press release announcing top-line results from its maintenance study of GLP-1/GIP agonist VK2735. A copy of the press release is filed as Exhibit 99.1 to this Current Report on Form 8-K and incorporated herein by reference. Item 9.01 Financial Statements and Exhibits. (d) Exhibits. Exhibit Number Description 99.1 Press Release, dated September 22, 2026. 104 Cover Page Interactive Data File, formatted in Inline Extensible Business Reporting Language (iXBRL). SIGNATURES Pursuant to the requirements of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934, the registrant has duly caused this report to be signed on its behalf by the undersigned hereunto duly authorized. VIKING THERAPEUTICS, INC. Date: September 22, 2026 By: /s/ Brian Lian, Ph.D. Brian Lian, Ph.D. President and Chief Executive Officer (Principal Executive Officer)\n\n[EX-99] EX-99.1 2 vktx-ex99_1.htm EX-99.1 EX-99.1 Exhibit 99.1 Viking Therapeutics Announces Positive Topline Results from Maintenance Study of GLP-1/GIP Agonist VK2735 Demonstrating the Promise of Multiple Maintenance Dosing Regimens 22% Placebo-Adjusted Weight Loss Reported at Week 33 Following Weekly Dosing of VK2735 at 17.5 mg; No Plateau Observed Results Demonstrate Viability of Monthly and Every Other Week Dosing Regimens for Maintaining Weight Loss; Increasing Options for Adherence to Treatment Up to 97% of Weight Loss Maintained Following Transition to Every Other Week Dosing for Three Months Up to 90% of Weight Loss Maintained Following Transition to Monthly Dosing for Three Months Excellent Tolerability Observed During Maintenance Dosing with GI Adverse Event Rates Similar to Placebo Conference Call Scheduled for 8:00 a.m. ET Today SAN DIEGO, CA &#x2013; September 22, 2026 &#x2013; Viking Therapeutics, Inc. (&#x201c;Viking&#x201d;) (NASDAQ: VKTX), a clinical-stage biopharmaceutical company focused on the development of novel therapies for metabolic and endocrine disorders, today announced positive top-line results from the company&#x2019;s maintenance study of VK2735, the company&#x2019;s dual agonist of the glucagon-like peptide 1 (GLP-1) and glucose-dependent insulinotropic polypeptide (GIP) receptors. In this study, subjects receiving subcutaneous VK2735 demonstrated superior weight maintenance following the transition to less frequent dosing regimens compared with subjects transitioned to placebo. In addition, VK2735 demonstrated an encouraging safety and tolerability profile during the 12-week maintenance dosing period, with observed rates of GI-related adverse events comparable to placebo. The company believes these results further differentiate VK2735 by demonstrating compelling weight loss maintenance via new long-term dosing regimens, including monthly and every-other-week administration. VK2735 is being developed in both subcutaneous and oral formulations for the potential treatment of various metabolic disorders such as obesity. The company plans to explore oral maintenance dosing regimens in an upcoming part 2 to the current study. &#x201c;The results of our innovative maintenance dosing study continue to demonstrate the significance of VK2735&#x2019;s unique and differentiated half-life and PK profile, which appear to enable an effective new approach to achieving and maintaining the weight loss goals of patients living with obesity,&#x201d; said Brian Lian, Ph.D., chief executive officer of Viking. &#x201c;We believe this dose-ranging study clearly demonstrated the potential viability of novel, extended dosing approaches for maintenance following induction with an incretin-based therapy. We believe flexible dosing approaches will provide both patients and their providers with new options for Exhibit 99.1 improving long-term adherence to therapy and sustained weight m", "headline_candidates_n": 1, "headline_article_cap": [], "fired_title_among_asked": true, "est_cost_usd_upper": 0.01922, "new_decision": null}
{"kind": "ticker_day", "ticker": "NHP", "date": "2026-09-28", "detectors": ["ep"], "old_paths": ["veto_516"], "old_match_paths": [], "old_grade": "strong", "old_decision": "PASS", "ep_day": true, "label": null, "arm": "ep: grader + headline", "corpus_source": "stored_grade_corpus", "corpus_len": 1055, "corpus": "[Benzinga 2026-09-28] National Healthcare Properties To Sell 40 Outpatient Medical Facilities For ~$531M; Announced Transactions Expected To Reduce Net Debt To Further Adjusted EBITDA To 0X Based On Q2 2026 Financials.\n\n[Web summary] NHP\u2019s gap-up was driven by its September 28 announcement that it had agreed to sell 40 outpatient medical facilities for about $531 million. The company expects roughly $511 million in cash proceeds and plans to use them to repay its revolving credit facility and fund senior-housing operating portfolio acquisitions.\n\nInvestors likely reacted to the larger strategic shift: including previously announced sales and a letter of intent for its final four facilities, NHP expects to exit outpatient medical properties and focus on senior housing. Management said the transactions could bring net debt to adjusted EBITDA to approximately zero, based on Q2 2026 financials. The 40-property sale is expected to close in Q4 2026, subject to customary conditions, so the proceeds and balance-sheet benefits are not yet realized.", "headline_candidates_n": 0, "headline_article_cap": [], "fired_title_among_asked": false, "est_cost_usd_upper": 0.01081, "new_decision": null}
{"kind": "ticker_day", "ticker": "IOVA", "date": "2026-09-29", "detectors": ["ep"], "old_paths": ["polygon_news"], "old_match_paths": ["title"], "old_grade": "strong", "old_decision": "BLOCK", "ep_day": true, "label": "operator 2026-10-01: wrongly blocked", "arm": "ep: grader + headline", "corpus_source": "stored_grade_corpus_first_6000", "corpus_len": 6000, "corpus": "[SEC 8-K filed 2026-09-29, items 8.01,9.01] false 0001425205 0001425205 2026-09-29 2026-09-29 0001425205 dei:FormerAddressMember 2026-09-29 2026-09-29 iso4217:USD xbrli:shares iso4217:USD xbrli:shares UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION WASHINGTON, D.C. 20549 FORM 8-K CURRENT REPORT Pursuant to Section 13 or 15(d) of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 Date of Report (Date of earliest event reported): September 29, 2026 IOVANCE BIOTHERAPEUTICS, INC. (Exact name of Registrant as Specified in Its Charter) Delaware 001-36860 75-3254381 (State or Other Jurisdiction of Incorporation) (Commission File Number) (IRS Employer Identification No.) 300 Rouse Blvd. Philadelphia , Pennsylvania 19112 (Address of Principal Executive Offices) (Zip Code) Registrant&#8217;s Telephone Number, Including Area Code: 650 260-7120 825 Industrial Road , Suite 100 San Carlos , California 94070 (Former Name or Former Address, if Changed Since Last Report) Check the appropriate box below if the Form 8-K filing is intended to simultaneously satisfy the filing obligation of the registrant under any of the following provisions: &#168; &#8239;&#8239;&#8239;Written communications pursuant to Rule 425 under the Securities Act (17 CFR 230.425) &#168; &#8239;&#8239;&#8239;&#8239;Soliciting material pursuant to Rule 14a-12 under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.14a-12) &#168; &#8239;&#8239;&#8239;&#8239;Pre-commencement communications pursuant to Rule 14d-2(b) under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.14d-2(b)) &#168; &#8239;&#8239;&#8239;&#8239;Pre-commencement communications pursuant to Rule 13e-4(c) under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.13e-4(c)) Securities registered pursuant to Section 12(b) of the Act: Title of each class Trading Symbol(s) Name of each exchange on which registered Common Stock, par value $0.000041666 IOVA The Nasdaq Global Market Indicate by check mark whether the registrant is an emerging growth company as defined in Rule 405 of the Securities Act of 1933 (&#167;&#8239;230.405 of this chapter) or Rule 12b-2 of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 (&#167;&#8239;240.12b-2 of this chapter). Emerging growth company &#168; If an emerging growth company, indicate by check mark if the registrant has elected not to use the extended transition period for complying with any new or revised financial accounting standards provided pursuant to Section 13(a) of the Exchange Act. &#168; Item 8.01 Other Events. On September 29, 2026, Iovance Biotherapeutics, Inc. issued a press release updating its full year 2026 revenue guidance. A copy of the press release is attached as Exhibit 99.1 and is incorporated herein by reference. Item 9.01 Financial Statements and Exhibits. (d) Exhibits. Exhibit No. Description 99.1 Press Release of Iovance Biotherapeutics, Inc., dated September 29, 2026 104 Cover Page Interactive Data File (embedded as Inline XBRL document) SIGNATURES Pursuant to the requirements of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934, the registrant has duly caused this report to be signed on its behalf by the undersigned hereunto duly authorized. Iovance Biotherapeutics, Inc. Date: September 29, 2026 By: /s/ Frederick G. Vogt Name: Frederick G. Vogt, Ph.D., J.D. Title: Interim CEO and President, and General Counsel\n\n[EX-99] EX-99.1 2 tm2626507d1_ex99-1.htm EXHIBIT 99.1 Exhibit 99.1 Iovance Biotherapeutics Raises Full Year 2026 Revenue Guidance to $410 to $420 Million New Guidance Represents an Increase of $55 Million at the Midpoint from the Prior Range of $350 to $370 Million Strong U.S. Demand for Amtagvi and Proleukin Drives Increased Outlook PHILADELPHIA, Pennsylvania, September 29, 2026 -- Iovance Biotherapeutics, Inc. (NASDAQ: IOVA), a commercial biotechnology company focused on innovating, developing, and delivering novel polyclonal tumor infiltrating lymphocyte (TIL) therapies for patients with cancer, today raised its full year 2026 total revenue guidance range to $410 to $420 million, driven by strong U.S. demand for Amtagvi&reg; (lifileucel) and Proleukin. The midpoint represents an increase of $55 million, or ~15%, over the previous guidance range of $350 to $370 million and implies nearly 60% annual growth in total revenue. &ldquo;Our record second quarter and sustained demand for Amtagvi and Proleukin led us to raise our full year 2026 total revenue guidance by $55 million at the midpoint,&rdquo; said Frederick Vogt, Ph.D., J.D., Interim President and Chief Executive Officer. &ldquo;Increasing patient demand and our current manufacturing schedule provide strong visibility into our third and fourth quarter revenues. In addition, lifileucel continues to advance across our registrational programs in new solid tumor indications, while continued manufacturing and operating efficiencies accelerate our progress toward profitability.&rdquo; Iovance most recently reported record second quarter 2026 total product revenue of $99.3 million, has grown its authorized treatment center (ATC) network to ~100 centers, and remains on track for expansion to at least 110 ATCs by year-end 2026. Iovance expects to report third quarter 2026 financial results in early November 2026. This update completes the guidance review announced with the Company&rsquo;s second quarter 2026 results. About&#8239;Iovance Biotherapeutics, Inc. Iovance Biotherapeutics, Inc. is the global leader in innovating, developing, and delivering tumor infiltrating lymphocyte (TIL) cell therapies for patients with solid tumors. Amtagvi&reg; (lifileucel) is the first FDA-approved, one-time treatment for previously treated advanced melanoma, now approved in three global markets and available at nearly 100 authorized treatment centers (ATCs). The Iovance TIL platform spans registrational trials and next-generation programs in additional solid tumors, including gene-edited and IL-12 tethered TIL therapies, next-generation IL-2, and precision immuno-oncology approaches. As the first and only company to take TIL therapy from concept to a broadly accessible commerci", "headline_candidates_n": 1, "headline_article_cap": [], "fired_title_among_asked": true, "est_cost_usd_upper": 0.01926, "new_decision": null}
{"kind": "ticker_day", "ticker": "NVTS", "date": "2026-09-29", "detectors": ["ep"], "old_paths": ["veto_516"], "old_match_paths": [], "old_grade": "routine", "old_decision": "PASS", "ep_day": true, "label": null, "arm": "ep: grader + headline", "corpus_source": "stored_grade_corpus", "corpus_len": 1052, "corpus": "[Benzinga 2026-09-28] Navitas Semiconductor Stock Surges After Hours: Here's Why. Navitas Semiconductor Corp (NASDAQ:NVTS) shares are soaring in extended trading Monday after the company was awarded the ALATTIS program.\n\n[Benzinga 2026-09-28] Navitas Selected By U.S. Gov To Develop Next-Gen 10kV SiC Power Semiconductors.\n\n[Web summary] NVTS gapped up after Navitas announced on September 28 that the U.S. Army selected it for the ALATTIS program, a prototype effort to develop and validate a domestic manufacturing process for next-generation 10 kV silicon-carbide power semiconductors for military and critical-infrastructure systems. The Army\u2019s selection followed a competitive evaluation.\n\nThe announcement sparked a sharp after-hours reaction, with reports of a roughly 14%\u201320% jump. The key caveat: Navitas did not disclose the program\u2019s funding, contract value, timeline, or expected revenue impact. So the immediate move reflects enthusiasm for the defense validation and potential future opportunity\u2014not a quantified near-term earnings boost.", "headline_candidates_n": 0, "headline_article_cap": [], "fired_title_among_asked": false, "est_cost_usd_upper": 0.01081, "new_decision": null}
{"kind": "ticker_day", "ticker": "SYNA", "date": "2026-10-02", "detectors": ["ep"], "old_paths": ["claude_classifier"], "old_match_paths": ["claude_classifier"], "old_grade": "mna", "old_decision": "BLOCK", "ep_day": true, "label": null, "arm": "ep: grader + headline", "corpus_source": "stored_grade_corpus_first_6000", "corpus_len": 6000, "corpus": "[SEC 8-K filed 2026-10-01, items 1.01,7.01,9.01] false 0000817720 0000817720 2026-10-01 2026-10-01 UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION Washington, D.C. 20549 FORM 8-K CURRENT REPORT Pursuant to Section 13 or 15(d) of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 Date of Report (Date of earliest event reported): October 1, 2026 SYNAPTICS INCORPORATED (Exact name of registrant as specified in its charter) Delaware 000-49602 77-0118518 (State or other jurisdiction of incorporation) (Commission File Number) (IRS Employer Identification No.) 1109 McKay Drive San Jose , California 95131 (Address of principal executive offices) (Zip Code) Registrant&#8217;s telephone number, including area code: ( 408 ) 904-1100 (Former Name or Former Address, if Changed Since Last Report) Check the appropriate box below if the Form 8-K filing is intended to simultaneously satisfy the filing obligations of the registrant under any of the following provisions: &#9744; Written communications pursuant to Rule 425 under the Securities Act (17 CFR 230.425) &#9746; Soliciting material pursuant to Rule 14a-12 under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.14a-12) &#9744; Pre-commencement communications pursuant to Rule 14d-2(b) under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.14d-2(b)) &#9744; Pre-commencement communications pursuant to Rule 13e-4(c) under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.13e-4(c)) Securities registered pursuant to Section 12(b) of the Act: Title of each class Trading Symbol(s) Name of each exchange on which registered Common stock, par value $0.001 per share SYNA NASDAQ Global Select Market Indicate by check mark whether the registrant is an emerging growth company as defined in Rule 405 of the Securities Act of 1933 (&#167;230.405 of this chapter) or Rule 12b-2 of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 (&#167;240.12b-2 of this chapter). Emerging growth company &#9744; If an emerging growth company, indicate by check mark if the registrant has elected not to use the extended transition period for complying with any new or revised financial accounting standards provided pursuant to Section 13(a) of the Exchange Act. &#9744; Item&#8201;1.01. Entry into a Material Definitive Agreement. On October 1, 2026, Synaptics Incorporated, a Delaware corporation (the &#8220; Company &#8221; or &#8220; Synaptics &#8221;), entered into an Amended and Restated Agreement and Plan of Merger (the &#8220; A&R Merger Agreement &#8221;), by and among the Company, ON Semiconductor Corporation, a Delaware corporation (&#8220; Parent &#8221; or &#8220; onsemi &#8221;), and Sonic Acquisition Corp., a Delaware corporation and wholly-owned subsidiary of Parent (&#8220; Merger Sub &#8221;), which amends and restates in its entirety the previously announced Agreement and Plan of Reorganization, dated as of June 25, 2026, by and among the Company, Merger Sub and Parent and continues to provide, among other things, that subject to the satisfaction or waiver of the conditions set forth therein, Merger Sub will merge with and into the Company (the &#8220; Merger &#8221;), with the Company surviving as an indirect, wholly-owned subsidiary of Parent. Capitalized terms used but not defined herein will have the meanings given to them in the A&R Merger Agreement. The A&R Merger Agreement was ultimately executed following negotiations arising from the Company receiving an unsolicited, non-binding proposal on September 2, 2026 from a strategic party, referred to as &#8220;Party A&#8221; in onsemi&#8217;s registration statement on Form S-4 (File No. 333-298477) previously filed on August 21, 2026, to acquire all the issued and outstanding shares of Company Common Stock (as defined below). Consistent with its fiduciary duties and in accordance with the terms of the Agreement and Plan of Reorganization, the Company&#8217;s Board of Directors (the &#8220; Company Board &#8221;), together with a special committee of independent directors of the Company Board previously formed for convenience and not as a result of any actual or perceived conflict of interest of a\n\n[EX-99] EX-99.2 4 ef20083029_ex99-2.htm EXHIBIT 99.2 Exhibit 99.2 SYNA Amended Offer All-Employee Email Subject: Today&#8217;s Announcement: An Amended Agreement with onsemi Team #OneSynaptics, I am writing to share an update regarding the acquisition of Synaptics by onsemi. Moments ago, we announced that Synaptics has amended its merger agreement with onsemi. Under the amended terms, Synaptics shareholders will receive $123 in cash for each share of Synaptics common stock held at the time of closing, which provides higher value and value certainty to our shareholders. We recognize that today&#8217;s announcement may raise questions about what has changed and how we arrived here. We entered our agreement with onsemi back in June, confident in the transaction&#8217;s reflection of the strength of our business model, our technology portfolio and our leadership position in intelligent edge processing and wireless connectivity. We believe the revised offer reflects onsemi's continued conviction in our business, our products and our people. The amended merger agreement was negotiated following the receipt of an unsolicited, non-binding proposal from a third party bidder. The Synaptics Board of Directors carefully evaluated that proposal, alongside our financial and legal advisors and in accordance with well-established governance procedures and the previously announced agreement with onsemi, and concluded that the onsemi transaction, as amended, continues to be in the best interests of Synaptics and its shareholders. As we&#8217;ve discussed since we initially launched our transaction with onsemi in June, we are excited about all of the opportunities we see ahead for our combined company. And while the terms of our agreement have changed, the strategic rationale for bringing Synaptics and onsemi together remains the same. Together, as a differentiated intelligent-edge platform, we expect to accelerate innovation, increas", "headline_candidates_n": 1, "headline_article_cap": [], "fired_title_among_asked": false, "est_cost_usd_upper": 0.01916, "new_decision": null}
